  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1130 PM CDT Tue May 26 2026\n\nAn Omega block will remain in place across the CONUS by the end of\nthe week with high pressure and drier air looming just to our\nnorth. A northwest to southeast moisture axis remains evident on\nguidance and this will be more than sufficient to foster\nadditional rain/storm chances into the weekend. PWs in this\nmoisture axis are progged to run 1.6-1.8\" which is above the 90th\npercentile this time of year. However, medium-range guidance \ncontinues to depict the high pressure/drier air mass gradually \nshifting south by Sunday which leads to decreasing PoPs that will\ncontinue into early next week. This should lend time to dry out \nafter repeated waves of drought-improving rainfall across Middle\nTennessee.",
